cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite the repository (and the technical report it accompanies)."
title: "edm-dropout-benchmark: Generative, Semi-Supervised and Fair Learning for Student-Dropout Prediction"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, multi-seed, significance-tested benchmark for student-dropout
  prediction on the UCI Realinho and OULAD datasets. A ten-phase pipeline (three
  supervised baselines, a hybrid-decoder tabular VAE and a TabDDPM diffusion
  oversampler, uncertainty- and DQN-based active learning, a self-labelled SSL
  baseline (Co-Forest), post-hoc and in-processing fairness, and a multimodal
  DistilBERT extension) plus a methodological-rigor layer (SMOTE baseline,
  bootstrap CIs, paired Wilcoxon tests with familywise correction, and a real-text
  validation). The recurring finding is that, on moderate-imbalance tabular data,
  the more elaborate levers do not beat a well-regularised supervised baseline; the
  contribution is the integrated, honest, reproducible evaluation. Extends four MDPI
  anchor papers from the Kotsiantis line (see docs/anchor_papers.md).
